    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Crowley are delighted to present this most exceptional residence, located 100 metres from the shoreline of Clew Bay on the outskirts of Westport town. \n\nWith a total floor area of approximately 260 sq m/ 2,777 sq ft this property would make an outstanding family home in an enviable location. Some of its attractive features include the high ceilings which enhance the feeling of space, cornicing in the ground floor rooms and oak internal doors, skirting and archtraving. \n\nBuilt in 2004, the architecturally designed house was completed to an excellent standard. It is entered through a substantial hallway opening to the right into the living room, from there the interconnecting dining room offers a very generous space for entertaining. The adjoining bright and well appointed kitchen/casual sitting room is enhanced by a triple aspect seating area with patio doors to the south facing terrace. Additional ground floor accommodation comprises of four large double en-suite bedrooms (main with walk-in wardrobe), office, sauna, bathroom, utility, cloakroom and WC. \n\nOn the first floor there are two double en-suite bedrooms, a study and WC. There is also a large, partially finished room which offers potential for a number of uses such as an additional living room, a superb home office or an additional bedroom. \n\nGardens:\nThis house is a gardener's dream, set on a secluded and beautifully landscaped site of approximately 0.62 acres, surrounded by hand built local stone walls and fronted by an electric gate. \n\nThe front garden features Liscannor stone terracing and pathways, manicured lawns, extensive mature planting of trees, shrubs and flowers, and ample parking on the gravel driveway. Both Croagh Patrick and the sea can be glimpsed through the surrounding mature woodlands.\n\nTo the rear is a substantial raised south-west facing terrace of non-slip porcelain paving (its base has been engineered to provide foundations for a future two storey extension if wished), an extensive brick paved patio, pond with fountain feature, and beautifully planted raised beds. This area is perfectly paced to catch the afternoon and evening sun and provides a superb space for al fresco dining during the summer months. \n\nTo the side of the house is a detached garage (5.45m x 3.05m) with electricity and a roller door, and a vegetable garden. A charming stone built canal has been constructed to house a meandering small stream with a stone archway and a border of raised flower beds. \n\nLocation:\nClooneen is one of Westport's most sought after residential areas. 1.8 km of coastal pedestrian pathway leads from the property past the Michelin Guide recommended Sheebeen Restaurant and Bar to Westport Quay and its many amenities including primary school, shops, restaurants/bars and hotel. For the sea swimming enthusiasts, there is a pebble beach just 200 metres from the property or a small pier 500 metres distance towards Westport Quay. Westport's vibrant town centre is a 3.5 km drive and some of Mayo's finest beaches are also to be found close by.\n\nOFFERS IN EXCESS OF 1,200,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 8.37m x 1.2m & 5.89m x 3.0m & 8.88m x 1.17m\nTiled floor, oak staircase\n\nLiving Room - 5.5m x 4.43m\nOak floor, timber and cast iron fireplace with gas fire, bay window, curtains\n\nDining Room - 4.43m x 4.05m\nOak floor, feature dual aspect corner window, timber and cast iron fireplace with gas fire, curtains\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 6.84m x 3.81m & 2.94m x 2.21m\nOak and tiled floors, triple aspect seating area, oak kitchen with granite countertops, island/breakfast bar, integrated gas hob, double electric oven, microwave and dishwasher, double doors to rear terrace\n\nUtility Room - 2.51m x 1.98m & 1.63m x 1.48m\nTiled floor, built in oak floor and wall units with sink, door to rear terrace\n\nOffice - 2.95m x 2.17m & 1.36m x 1.21m\nOak laminate floor, built in shelving and storage\n\nWC - 1.99m x 1.24m\nTiled floor, wc, whb\n\nBedroom One - 4.75m x 4.43m\nOak floor, bay window with a glimpse of the sea, curtains and blinds\n\nWalk-in Wardrobe - 2.26m x 0.98m\nOak floor\n\nEn-Suite - 3.29m x 1.5m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nCloakroom - 2.07m x 0.98m\nOak floor, shelving\n\nBedroom Two - 3.95m x 3.3m & 1.17m x 0.96m\nOak floor, built in wardrobes, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 3.29m x 1.18m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nBedroom Three - 4.22m x 3.3m & 1.15m x 0.78m\nOak floor, built in wardrobes, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 2.01m x 1.59m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nBedroom Four - 4.03m x 3.32m & 1.08m x 0.99m\nOak floor, built in wardrobes, blinds\n\nEn-Suite - 2.66m x 1.17m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nBathroom - 3.07m x 1.76m & 2.09m x 1.49m\nFully tiled, jacuzzi bath, wc, whb\n\nSauna - 1.11m x 0.95m\nCanadian cedar sauna installed in 2024, with wifi\n\nHotpress/Plant Room - 1.43m x 1.03m\nShelved\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 6.17m x 1.63m & 7.12m x 0.9m & 4.1m x 0.9m\nGallery landing with oak floor, velux window\n\nBedroom Five - 5.04m x 3.06m & 1.97m x 0.65m\nFrench pine floor, velux windows with blinds, attic access\n\nEn-Suite - 1.84m x 1.7m\nFully tiled, shower, wc, whb\n\nPotential Additional Living Room - 7.0m x 5.0m\nPartially finished room with pine clad ceiling, velux windows x 3\n\nBedroom 6 - 4.46m x 4.43m\nFrench pine floor, velux\n\nEn-Suite - 3.43m x 1.13m & 0.83m x 0.77m\nTiled floor and part tiled walls, shower, wc, whb\n\nOffice - 2.22m x 1.48m & 1.6m x 1.24m\nOak floor, velux\n\nWC - 1.45m x 1.34m\nTiled floor, wc, whb\n\n"
